{
  "_comment": "Permission rules the runtime's own scripts need to run unattended. `bin/permit apply` merges them, with the project's own rules (<repo>/.maxxfactory/permissions.json: checks, deploys, DNS, mail, MCP tools the approved plan needs, added with `bin/permit add`), into the settings; the owner types it once. Each script is listed under both path spellings (~ and the absolute home; {HOME} is replaced), because rules match the start of the command line and auto mode drops path wildcards. Outward actions (publishing, deploying, DNS, sending mail, merging to the default branch) are not here: they are pre-allowed per project, each as a row of the plan's `Pre-authorized actions` table that the owner approved. Never pre-allowed: paying for credits or plans, deleting data, a repository, or a production resource.",
